**Status:** M1 (schema) + M2 (read RPCs + shell) + M3 (cell drawer + variance badges) + M4 (parallel writes) + M5 (re-open) shipped. Pending polish: row/col virtualization with @tanstack/react-virtual, batched HR-PMS-override notifications, E16 auto-revert cron.

**Master switch:** `admin_feature_flags.feature_bulk_review_dashboard` (default `false`). Off = sidebar entry hidden + RPCs throw `feature disabled`. `mgmt_can_reopen` (default `false`) controls whether Management can re-open vs Admin-only.

**Gradual rollout (May 2026):** `admin_feature_flags` now carries `target_roles app_role[]` and `target_user_ids uuid[]`. Both empty = enabled for everyone when value=true. Non-empty = enabled only for matching role OR explicit user. **Admins always bypass targeting** once master switch is ON. Evaluation centralised in SECURITY DEFINER RPC `is_feature_flag_enabled_for_me(p_key)`; the client hook `useBulkReviewFlag` calls this RPC (do NOT re-evaluate targeting in the SDK). Admin UI lives at Admin → Settings → **Feature Flags** (`FeatureFlagsTab.tsx`).

**§0 Non-Regression Contract (LOCKED):**
- Strictly additive: no existing column/RPC signature/RLS policy/notification template modified.
- New route `/review/bulk-scoring` only. Legacy `/dashboard?view=*` paths byte-identical.
- New tables auto-included in backup via `get_backup_table_order()` (no allowlist edit).
- POLICY §88 preserved: post-approval mutations only via `final_score_revisions` rows.
- Rollback = flip flag OFF; new columns retain defaults, new tables stay populated but unread.

**Schema (M1):**
- `kpis.kpi_group_type` ∈ {`individual`|`departmental`|`org`}, default `individual`
- `review_submissions`: `is_group_override`, `group_write_batch_id`, `is_auditor_override_of_hr`, `skipped_by_management JSONB`, `final_revision_no INT`, `row_version INT` (E9 concurrency)
- Tables: `admin_feature_flags`, `bulk_review_batches`, `final_score_revisions`
- All writes to bulk tables go through SECURITY DEFINER RPCs only — no direct INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE policies.

**RPCs (M2 read-side):**
- `bulk_scope_preview(p_period, p_year, p_filters)` — counts + cap check (25k cells / 5MB)
- `bulk_review_snapshot(p_period, p_year, p_viewer_stage, p_filters, p_page, p_page_size DEFAULT 200, max 500)`
- `kpi_cell_detail(p_kpi_id, p_emp_id)` — per-click only. Returns `{ kpi, submission, revisions, employee, kpi_history{kpis,submissions}, queries, workflow, org_kpi }` so the drawer can render the **same `KpiReviewPanel`** as "View KPI Details" (rating-scale-derived rating, evidence links, history, queries, journey). Lean-load (ADR-064/066) preserved — grid never pre-fetches this payload.
- All flag-gated (`is_bulk_review_enabled()`) + role-gated (admin/manager/skip_level/hr_pms/auditor/management).
- Daily-frequency KPIs excluded (E12).

**Frontend invariants:**
- `useBulkReviewFlag` drives sidebar visibility + route gate.
- Page mounts empty; `bulk_scope_preview` only when flag ON; `bulk_review_snapshot` only after explicit Load Scope click (`scopeLoaded` state).
- 25k cell / 5MB cap disables Load button via `preview.cap_exceeded`.
- No realtime; manual Refresh pill only; SWR 5min.

**Stakeholder defaults (locked):**
- Flag default OFF for every tenant.
- `mgmt_can_reopen` default false (admin-granted only).
- E16: auto-revert at period close with `auto_reverted=true` revision row.
- Variance badge: fixed 1.0 absolute on 0–5 rating.

**Pending milestones:**
**Write RPCs (M4):**
- `bulk_write_stage_scores(p_stage, p_cells, p_batch_reason)` — per-stage column write, skips cells with `final_score IS NOT NULL` (Policy §88), rejects HR PMS write when `auditor_score IS NOT NULL`, enforces `expected_row_version` (E9), stamps `group_write_batch_id` + `row_version+1` + `bulk_review_batches` audit row with skip reasons.
- `bulk_management_approve(p_cells, p_batch_reason)` — picks `final_score` from highest-priority completed stage (auditor>hr_pms>skip_level>manager), records `skipped_by_management` JSONB, requires `ConfirmDestructiveDialog`.

**Re-open (M5):**
- `bulk_reopen_cells(p_cells, p_stages_to_unlock, p_reason)` — Admin always; Management only when `is_mgmt_reopen_enabled()` is true. Reason min 8 chars. Inserts `final_score_revisions` row, bumps `final_revision_no`, NULLs `final_score` + selected stage scores, increments `row_version`.

**Frontend (M3/M4/M5):**
- `BulkCellDrawer` (Sheet) shows stage strip, variance badge, write form (gated to viewer stage + non-final), re-open form (gated to admin/management + final), raw audit JSON.
- Dashboard adds row selection + sticky "Bulk Approve (Mgmt)" toolbar (admin+management only) with `ConfirmDestructiveDialog`. Row variance Δ badge inline.

**Phase 2 polish (shipped):**
- Row virtualization: `BulkReviewVirtualGrid` uses `@tanstack/react-virtual` with CSS-grid column template, overscan 12, sticky header, 36px row height. Replaces the legacy `<table>` rendering in the dashboard.
- HR-PMS override notification: `bulk_write_stage_scores` counts cells where `hr_pms_score IS NOT NULL` at write time and (when stage = `auditor`) inserts one `notifications` row per active HR PMS user, `type = 'auditor_override_of_hr'`, metadata = `{ batch_id, affected_count, period, year, deep_link }`. Wrapped in `EXCEPTION WHEN OTHERS THEN NULL` so the notification step can never roll back the underlying score write.

**E16 auto-revert (M5):**
- Edge function `bulk-review-auto-revert` scans `final_score_revisions` rows with `new_final_score IS NULL` and reverts them to `prev_final_score` once the underlying `(review_period, review_year)` is globally locked or `current_stage='closed'`. Stamps the revision with `auto_reverted=true` and `new_final_score=prev_final_score` so the audit row is closed immutably. Daily cron, x-cron-secret guarded, 2000-row chunk.

**Matrix mode reachability (v2.66.12.5):**
- `useBulkReviewSnapshotAll` loops `bulk_review_snapshot` pages (`p_page_size=500`) until exhausted on Load Scope; hard guard at 60 pages (30k cells). Pre-`bulk_scope_preview` 25k-cell cap (POLICY §0) still gates the Load button so the loop never runs away.
- Matrix renders **every mapped employee as a column** with horizontal scroll inside the matrix surface; the `KPI / KRA` column is frozen (sticky-left) and the employee header row is sticky-top. No employee windowing/pager — `EmployeeWindowPager` removed in v2.66.12.6. Fixed column widths (KPI 260px, Employee 112px) keep the layout usable at 100% browser zoom; the 25k-cell scope cap still bounds total render cost. **v2.66.12.7 polish:** sticky KPI cells carry an opaque zebra background (`bg-card` / `bg-muted/30`) so columns don't bleed through; scroll container uses `.matrix-scroll` class (defined in `src/index.css`, themed `::-webkit-scrollbar` from `--muted`/`--muted-foreground` tokens + `scroll-behavior: smooth`); each KPI row sets `content-visibility: auto` + `contain-intrinsic-size: 56px` to skip paint for off-screen rows on large matrices.
- KRA filter (`useBulkReviewKraOptions`) cascades from Category and is applied **client-side** on the accumulated rows — RPC signature unchanged. Selection resets when Category / Period / Year changes.
